## 0. TL;DR (Decision Snapshot)

</aside>

**Who is impacted:**
India’s 300+ million informal, gig, and first-time earners in Delhi NCR who are financially active but excluded by language, documentation complexity, and distrust of formal financial products.

**Problem:**
No financial product today serves users with variable income, no employer documentation, and a deep distrust of schemes — in their language, at their literacy level, with their employment reality as the baseline.

**Why now:**
65% of gig workers have no insurance (Borzo 2024). 90% lack any savings (NITI Aayog 2024). 30 crore are registered on eShram but have never received a single benefit. The Account Aggregator framework now exists to solve the onboarding problem. Sarvam AI makes Hindi voice AI viable. The infrastructure window is open; the competitive window is not yet closed.

**Solution:**
DhanSathi is an AI-powered financial companion — a three-tab product (Insurance, Investment, Borrowing) with a Hindi voice agent (Vaani), an Account Aggregator-backed tracker, and a scheme enrollment engine that handles documentation. First session to first enrollment: under 15 minutes.

**Expected impact:**
10,000 active Delhi users in 6 months post-launch. Session 1 enrollment completion at 40%+. Day-30 retention at 25%+. LTV:CAC ratio of 2.0 at 10% monthly churn (Month 12 target).

