### US-01 — Income and Transaction Detection

**Story:** As a user, I want the app to detect my income and transactions from my history, so that I get personalized guidance without filling out a long form.

**Story Points:** 8 · **Priority:** P0 (Must Have)

**Functional Requirements:**

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| FR-01-01 | System should present income type selection (Delivery partner, Domestic work, Office job, My business, Freelance and contract) as the first screen after language selection |
| FR-01-02 | User should be able to link their bank account via Account Aggregator (RBI-regulated) with explicit consent screen shown before any data access |
| FR-01-03 | Consent screen must display in Hindi and English: exact data scope (“DhanSathi will read your last 6 months of transaction history”), purpose, and revocation rights |
| FR-01-04 | System should ingest transaction data via Account Aggregator API and derive: estimated monthly income, income pattern (fixed or variable), major expense categories, approximate savings buffer |
| FR-01-05 | If Account Aggregator consent is declined, system should proceed with manual income input (single field: “What is your approximate monthly income?”) as a fallback |
| FR-01-06 | User should be able to edit their income type and manual income at any time from profile settings |
| FR-01-07 | Derived financial profile should update automatically whenever a new Account Aggregator data refresh is triggered (minimum monthly cadence) |

**Non-Functional Requirements:**

| ID | NFR |
| --- | --- |
| NFR-01-01 | Account Aggregator data fetch should complete in under 5 seconds on a 4G connection |
| NFR-01-02 | No raw Aadhaar or bank credentials are stored by DhanSathi at any point; AA tokens are stored encrypted |
| NFR-01-03 | AA consent revocation should propagate within 24 hours and trigger data deletion |

**Acceptance Criteria (Story-Level — US-01):**

- [ ]  User can complete onboarding from income type selection to dashboard in under 4 minutes without manual income entry when AA consent is given
- [ ]  AA-derived income and expense summary appears on the dashboard within 5 seconds of consent confirmation on a 4G connection
- [ ]  If AA consent is declined, the manual income fallback is presented without error and onboarding continues normally to the dashboard

**Modules:**

**M1.1 — Income Type Selection Module**
Screen presenting 5 income type options as selectable cards (not a form dropdown). Selected income type is stored in user profile and is used as the primary filter for scheme eligibility. User flow: App open → Language selection → Income type selection → [Continue].

