### US-03 — Government Scheme Eligibility Display

**Story:** As a user, I want to see which government schemes I already qualify for, so that I know what protection or benefits I’m currently missing.

**Story Points:** 13 · **Priority:** P0 (Must Have)

**Functional Requirements:**

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| FR-03-01 | System should match user profile (income, employment type, age, family size, existing schemes, risk tier) against eligibility criteria for a minimum of 15 government schemes at MVP launch |
| FR-03-02 | Scheme list should show only schemes the user qualifies for, with ineligible schemes suppressed |
| FR-03-03 | Each scheme card should display: scheme name in Hindi and English, cost (annual premium or zero), benefit in plain language (e.g., “Rs. 2 lakh accident cover”), enrollment time estimate |
| FR-03-04 | Scheme eligibility criteria must be sourced only from MyScheme API (NIC) or equivalent official government data source; no manually curated eligibility rules |
| FR-03-05 | System should surface the lowest-cost, highest-coverage scheme first within each category (Insurance, Loan, Health) |
| FR-03-06 | Scheme data must refresh at minimum weekly from the official source |

**Non-Functional Requirements:**

| ID | NFR |
| --- | --- |
| NFR-03-01 | Scheme eligibility matching should complete in under 2 seconds for a given user profile |
| NFR-03-02 | Scheme data must be versioned; old eligibility rules should be preserved for enrolled users |

**Acceptance Criteria (Story-Level — US-03):**

- [ ]  System returns only schemes the user qualifies for based on their profile — zero ineligible schemes appear in the list for any test profile
- [ ]  Scheme list renders within 2 seconds for any user profile on a 4G connection
- [ ]  All scheme eligibility criteria are sourced from MyScheme API (NIC) or an equivalent official government data source — no manually authored eligibility rules in production code

**Modules:**

**M2.1 — Scheme Eligibility Engine Module**
Rules-based matching engine. Input: user profile object (income, income_type, age, family_size, existing_schemes, location, risk_tier). Output: ranked list of eligible scheme objects with enrollment status. Integrates with MyScheme API (NIC) for live eligibility criteria. Falls back to cached criteria if API is unavailable. User flow: User opens Insurance or Borrowing tab → Profile loaded → Eligibility engine runs → Eligible scheme list rendered.

