### US-09 — Scheme Update Notifications

**Story:** As a user, I want to be notified when a new scheme becomes relevant to my profile, so that I don’t miss support because I didn’t know it existed.

**Story Points:** 5 · **Priority:** P1 (Should Have)

**Functional Requirements:**

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| FR-09-01 | System should run a background scheme eligibility re-check every 7 days for each active user |
| FR-09-02 | If a new scheme is added to the eligibility engine AND the user qualifies for it, a push notification should be sent within 24 hours |
| FR-09-03 | Notification message must name the scheme and state the benefit in one sentence: “A new scheme you qualify for: PMJJBY — Rs. 2 lakh life cover for Rs. 436/year” |
| FR-09-04 | Tapping the notification must deep-link directly to the scheme detail screen |
| FR-09-05 | User should be able to manage notification preferences from settings (scheme alerts on/off) |

**Modules:**

**M2.4 — Push Notification Module (Scheme Alerts)**
Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) integration for push notifications. Background job (Cloud Function) runs weekly eligibility re-check per user. Notification payload includes scheme_id, scheme_name, benefit_summary, deep_link. Hindi and English notification body based on user language preference. User flow: Background job runs → New scheme detected for user profile → FCM payload dispatched → User receives push → Taps → Scheme detail screen.

