### US-06 — Liquid Investment with Penalty-Free Withdrawal

**Story:** As a user, I want to invest and withdraw my savings at any time without penalty, so that my money stays available for emergencies rather than locked into a fixed term.

**Story Points:** 5 · **Priority:** P0 (Must Have)

**Functional Requirements:**

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| FR-07-01 | Investment tab must display only products where exit is possible within 7 calendar days with no principal loss, by default for Conservative and Moderate risk tiers |
| FR-07-02 | Each investment card must display: product name, annual return (%), exit timeline (e.g. “Withdraw within 1–2 business days”), minimum investment amount, regulatory body |
| FR-07-03 | Risk tier label must be visible on the tab (“Your profile: Conservative — liquid options shown”) with an option to change the risk tier |
| FR-07-04 | Investment flow must include: amount input (minimum Rs. 500), confirmation screen showing projected 1-month and 1-year return, bank debit confirmation |
| FR-07-05 | Post-investment, the user’s portfolio should be visible in the dashboard as a summary card |
| FR-07-06 | Withdrawal request must be completable in under 3 taps from the portfolio view |
| FR-07-07 | System must show “Withdraw within X business days” language prominently on every investment card and on the investment confirmation screen — never show it as a footnote |

**Non-Functional Requirements:**

| ID | NFR |
| --- | --- |
| NFR-07-01 | Investment product data must come from verified, SEBI-regulated sources only (AMC APIs or AMFI data) |
| NFR-07-02 | Payment initiation must use UPI (Razorpay or Cashfree) and must not store card or bank credentials |

**Modules:**

**M4.1 — Liquid Investment Options Module**
Connects to AMFI/AMC data feed for live NAV and fund metadata. Filters by user risk tier and exit timeline (less than or equal to 7 days). Renders as card list ranked by return. User flow: Investment tab → Risk tier badge → Product list → Card tapped → Detail screen → [Invest].

**Figma wireframe:** Screen S9 — Investment Tab

https://www.figma.com/design/Vhz7DU9cHXZgzS1r2rMTP1/DhanSathi---User-Flow-Wireframes

**M4.2 — Risk-Tier Investment Filter Module**
Client-side filter applied to product list based on user’s risk_tier from profile. Conservative: overnight and liquid funds only. Moderate: liquid, ultra-short term funds. Growth: includes short-term debt funds. Filter change prompt asks one question (“Are you comfortable with a 30-day lock-in?”) before allowing Growth tier access.

**M4.3 — Investment Action Module**
Amount input → projected returns calculator (simple: amount × annual_rate / 12) → UPI payment initiation → Confirmation screen → Portfolio updated. Handles payment failure with retry flow and clear error messaging. User flow: Product card → [Invest] → Amount input → Return preview → [Confirm] → UPI deeplink → Payment confirmed → Portfolio updated.

**Figma wireframe:** Screen S10 — Investment Detail

https://www.figma.com/design/Vhz7DU9cHXZgzS1r2rMTP1/DhanSathi---User-Flow-Wireframes

