## 8. EPIC 6 — Vaani Voice Agent

</aside>

**Epic description:** Vaani is the AI conversational layer that makes DhanSathi accessible to users who cannot or will not navigate traditional app interfaces. She answers questions, guides enrollments, performs the borrowing check, and provides personalized recommendations — in Hindi, within 5 questions per session, always ending with one specific actionable recommendation.

**Business value:** Vaani is the product’s primary differentiator. No existing financial app in India serves the informal worker segment with a Hindi voice agent. Every Vaani session that completes is a trust event. Every session that fails is a churn event.

**Success metrics:**

| Metric | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Vaani session start rate (% of active users who start a session) | 50%+ in first week |
| Vaani session completion rate (recommendation received) | 70%+ |
| Median questions per session | 3–4 (maximum 5) |
| User satisfaction with Vaani response (thumbs-up rate) | 75%+ |

---

### US-05 (Vaani component) + US-07 — Voice Agent Recommendation Session

**Story 1:** As a user, I want to complete scheme enrollment through a Hindi voice-guided flow, so that I don’t need to read English forms or visit a government office.

**Story 2 (Should Have):** As a user, I want the voice assistant to ask me up to 5 questions and give me one specific recommendation, so that I get guided advice without having to navigate the app myself.

**Story Points:** 13 (combined) · **Priority:** P0 for voice enrollment, P1 for recommendation session

**Functional Requirements:**

| ID | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| FR-08-01 | Vaani must respond in the user’s language: Hindi if user speaks Hindi, English if user speaks English, within the same session |
| FR-08-02 | Each Vaani session must not exceed 5 questions before producing a recommendation or action |
| FR-08-03 | Vaani must read all data already present in the user profile before asking any question; questions must only fill information gaps, never re-ask confirmed data |
| FR-08-04 | Every Vaani session must end with one specific recommendation and a single actionable next step: “I suggest you enroll in PMSBY. It costs Rs. 20 per year. Want me to start the enrollment now?” |
| FR-08-05 | Vaani must never use financial jargon without a plain-language explanation in the same sentence |
| FR-08-06 | If a user’s Vaani session is interrupted (call, app background), the session state must be preserved for 10 minutes; user should be able to resume |
| FR-08-07 | Vaani must never recommend a product that requires locking money beyond the user’s stated {lock_in_tolerance}. Default to zero lock-in products unless user has explicitly specified otherwise |
| FR-08-08 | Vaani must include an escape to human support: “अगर आपको अभी किसी इंसान से बात करनी है, तो यहाँ tap करें” — always visible as a secondary option |

**Non-Functional Requirements:**

| ID | NFR |
| --- | --- |
| NFR-08-01 | STT transcription latency must be under 2 seconds on a 4G connection |
| NFR-08-02 | Claude API response (recommendation generation) must complete in under 4 seconds |
| NFR-08-03 | TTS audio playback must begin streaming within 1 second of Claude response completion |
| NFR-08-04 | All voice data must be processed in-session and not stored permanently; transcripts may be retained for 30 days for support purposes only |

**Modules:**

**M6.1 — STT/TTS Module (Sarvam AI)**
Integrates Sarvam AI Saarika-v2 for Hindi STT (speech-to-text) and Sarvam Bulbul-v1 for TTS (text-to-speech). Handles microphone permissions, audio buffering, and real-time transcription. Falls back to text input if microphone unavailable or STT confidence is below 70%. User flow: Vaani session starts → Mic opens → User speaks → STT transcription → Passed to Claude → Claude response → TTS playback → Next question or recommendation.

**M6.2 — Claude API Conversation Engine Module**
System prompt defines Vaani’s persona, session constraints (5-question cap, single recommendation, lock_in_tolerance rule, Hindi-first rule, jargon rule). User profile injected into system prompt at session start: {income_type, monthly_income, family_size, risk_tier, existing_schemes, last_3_transactions_summary, expense_appetite, lock_in_tolerance}. Claude manages conversation state within the session context. Tool calls available: scheme_lookup(scheme_id), investment_filter(risk_tier, max_lock_in_days), savings_check(user_id). Model: claude-sonnet-4-6.

**M6.3 — Session State Management Module**
Stores active Vaani session state in Firebase Realtime Database: session_id, user_id, session_context (array of question-answer pairs), current_question_number, session_type (insurance, investment, borrowing, general), timestamp. Session expires after 10 minutes of inactivity. Resumes on return if within expiry window.

**M6.4 — Recommendation Output Module**
Parses Claude’s final recommendation JSON: {recommendation_type, product_id, product_name, action_required, action_label, action_deep_link, confidence_score}. Renders as a structured card: recommendation summary in Hindi, action button (e.g., “PMSBY में Enroll करें”), optional detail expansion. Routes to enrollment or investment flow on action button tap.

**Figma wireframe:** Screen S7 — Vaani Session (voice interface and recommendation card context)

https://www.figma.com/design/Vhz7DU9cHXZgzS1r2rMTP1/DhanSathi---User-Flow-Wireframes

**Acceptance Criteria (Story-Level — US-07, Vaani Recommendation Session):**

- [ ]  Vaani session reaches a recommendation in 5 or fewer questions for all test scenarios across insurance, investment, and borrowing contexts — no session requires a 6th question
- [ ]  Recommendation output renders as a structured card with product name, benefit summary in Hindi, and a single actionable CTA button
- [ ]  When the app is backgrounded mid-session, conversation state is preserved and a "Resume your session?" prompt appears on return within the 10-minute window

