<aside>

## 15. Out of Scope (Explicit Deferrals)

</aside>

This PRD does not include:

- **Income and expense auto-categorization:** Deferred to post-MVP. Requires reliable transaction tagging API and is explicitly conditional on API availability (marked as Could Have in user stories, requires AA data with category metadata).
- **WhatsApp first-session and in-app WhatsApp channel:** Future scope. Requires WhatsApp Business API integration and is V2 product architecture.
- **Daily, weekly, or monthly digest notifications:** Deferred. Not required for Session 1 value delivery; adds complexity to the notification system without MVP-critical impact.
- **iOS build:** Android-only at MVP. iOS requires separate build pipeline and additional store compliance work.
- **Tax filing (ITR):** Explicitly out of scope. Seasonal use case; Cleartax owns this. Addressed in Won’t Have user stories.
- **Loan marketplace:** Explicitly out of scope. Requires lending license, 6+ months of behavioral data for underwriting, and conflicts with guidance-only V1 positioning. Addressed in Won’t Have user stories.
- **Advanced investment portfolio analytics:** Post-MVP. Basic portfolio view (balance, projected return) is in scope; charts, benchmarks, and performance history are not.
- **Family plan and multi-user accounts:** V2 feature. Mentioned as a CLV lever in Section E but not required for MVP.
- **Suresh segment’s interest rate simulator:** Could Have, not built at MVP due to AMFI API complexity and low first-session conversion value relative to the Insurance tab.

